From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:16:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: transcode BC3 alpha, BC4 and BC5 through an endpoint
 pair table

The BC1-BC5 lowmem transcoder (csf-v11/197-203) loses to RC4-lowmem's
precompiled kernels on the G615 (upload_gpu_ms BC1 3.45 vs 2.89,
BC3 4.33 vs 3.22, BC4S 2.66 vs 1.17, BC5U 3.96 vs 2.50). It uses 53-59
registers (one thread per slot), and the EAC part searched 16 EAC_NEAR
loads per channel.

A BC4 block's palette depends only on its two endpoint bytes, so the
EAC (base, multiplier, table) that fits it and the EAC index of every
palette entry do too. panvk_bc_eac_lutgen.c (offline, idea and
exact-end rule adapted from GunaCharanTeja/panvk-kbase-android
csf-v11/213 and 219, MIT) fits all 65536 pairs per EAC kind (alpha, R11,
signed R11; multiplier 0 for R11; a fit keeps an exact 0 / max level
when the palette has one). The driver expands a kind's 16-bit headers
with the palette entry -> index map into a 512 KiB BO at its first use
(push constant lut). The shader does one load per block and remaps the
16 BC indices.

Valhall v11 (tools/spvstat), cycles / registers, bc3 -> this:
  BC4U 30.0/53 -> 10.3/16, BC4S 29.8/55 -> 10.3/16,
  BC5U 54.3/57 -> 14.7/19, BC5S 53.8/57 -> 14.7/19,
  BC3 81.1/59 -> 54.5/59, BC1 58.3/59 -> 50.6/59 (with the opts below).
BC4/BC5 now fit in 32 registers (2 threads).

Default PANVK_BC_LM_OPTS goes from 0x30000 to 0x20000: no ETC2 planar
mode (-0.7 dB on gradients, a sixth of the BC1 cycles), and the H mode
only on blocks whose ETC1 error is above 1024 (-0.01 dB). New bits:
0x400000 EAC by the old search, 0x800000 H on every block.
PANVK_BC_LM_OPTS=0xc30000 is the csf-v11/203 encoder, bit-identical.

Quality (tools/bc-bench, 1024^2, PSNR vs the exact BC decode, bc3 ->
this): BC1 random 20.19 -> 20.19, gradient 41.17 -> 40.46; BC3
25.80/42.30 -> 25.88/41.6; BC4U 33.26/52.19 -> 35.40/51.71; BC4S
33.21/40.28 -> 35.42/40.82; BC5U 33.26/51.92 -> 35.42/51.21; BC5S
33.22/40.37 -> 35.39/42.47.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
